.Dd 2021-02-11               \" DATE 
.Dt json_format 1      \" Program name and manual section number 
.Os UNIX/Linux/Darwin
.Sh NAME                 \" Section Header - required - don't modify 
.Nm json_format
.\" The following lines are read in generating the apropos(man -k) database. Use only key
.\" words here as the database is built based on the words here and in the .ND line. 
.\" .Nm Other_name_for_same_program(),
.\" .Nm Yet another name for the same program.
.\" Use .Nm macro to designate other names for the documented program.
.Nd JSON formatter, validator, and swiss army knife.
.Sh SYNOPSIS             \" Section Header - required - don't modify
.Nm
.\" .Op Fl abcd          \" [-abcd]
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl t
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl n Ar name         \" [-p port] 
.Op Fl s Ar schema       \" [-p port] 
.Op Fl f Ar format       \" [-P httpport] 
.\" .Op Ar                   \" [file ...]
.\" .Ar arg0                 \" Underlined argument - use .Ar anywhere to underline
.\" arg2 ...                 \" Arguments
files ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION          \" Section Header - required - don't modify
.Nm
formats, transforms and validates JSON files.
.Pp
If
.Ar files
are omitted,
.Pa stdin
is used instead.  Use redirection to put output into files.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "this much"
.It Fl q
Quiet.  When using the
.Fl s
option to perform validation, do not render a success message.
.It Fl t
Tidy JSON files.  This adjusts the indenting to 2 spaces per level, using
all spaces.  Comments in the input are lost.  If
compiled with
.Fl DPARSNIP_DICTIONARY_SORTED ,
object properties will be written in sorted order.
.It Fl x
Explain JSON schemas.  Parameters are JSON schemas, each of which is loaded
and explanatory text provided describine the document structure, value
ranges and types, etc.
.It Fl f Ar format
Flatten JSON files into a series of definitions, facilitating shell access
or comparison of contents.
.Ar format
is either
.Li dictionary ,
which renders JSON object properties with array syntax,
or
.Li member ,
which renders them as structure-member syntax (dot-name).
Objects with no properties and arrays with no elements lose any representation.
If compiled with
.Fl DPARSNIP_DICTIONARY_SORTED ,
object properties will be written in sorted order, making it possible to
apply tools such as
.Xr diff 1 .
.It Fl n Ar name
Use
.Ar name
as the variable name for
.Fl f ,
or as the descriptive text with
.Fl x .
If omitted, the filename is used instead.
.It Fl s Ar schema
Specifies a schema which is used to validate the specified files.
.El                      \" Ends the list
.Pp
